{
 "_about": [
  "Geometry for the RGA clearance check of the RIKEN BDR Fluent 780 (io/fluent/rga_clearance.py). Millimetres, deck",
  "coordinates of FluentControl (X to the right, Y to the back, Z up). Positions are TCP (tool centre point) positions",
  "of the RGA: the point between the finger tips at the grip height.",
  "Sources (only numbers derived from them are kept here):",
  "- log: the RGA move lines of FluentControl's log of 2026-11-17 and 2026-11-18 (PostPath / PrePath points, 'Move is",
  "  finished' positions): site positions, grip heights, C and gripper widths.",
  "- dump: the collision model FluentControl's PathFinder dumped for the RGA (X3D, layout of 2025-05): the RGA parts",
  "  (relative to the TCP; u = TCP -> rotation axis, C=180: +X, C=90: -Y; v = u turned by +90 degrees; z above the",
  "  TCP) and the boxes of the deck objects.",
  "- definitions: FluentControl's definition files: the base worktable WT2411004293_Ver.0.5_OFML (which carrier and",
  "  labware stands on which site, the order of the sites), the site templates (taught RobotPaths: approach and grip",
  "  waypoints per grip type, relative to the site) and the component templates (dimensions).",
  "- A grip height is the site's reference height plus the last waypoint of its taught path; the reference height is",
  "  calibrated on a logged grip at that site template. The path belongs to the site, not to the labware, so a plate",
  "  of another type at the same site is gripped at the same height.",
  "status: 'measured' = read from the log or the dump; 'derived' = computed from the definitions and calibrated",
  "values, not yet observed on the instrument; 'estimated' = derived from measured values with a further assumption;",
  "'assumed' = not verified (listed in README, section RGA clearance check).",
  "Validated against 11 real events (5 collisions, 6 clear moves; tests/io/fluent/test_rga_clearance.py)."
 ],
